    "essential_omission": false,
    "accepted_production_losses": [
      "Definitions, principle statements and explanations become recognition rather than independently composed prose. This review does not certify unaided production of any original written answer.",
      "The maxima/minima unit supplies candidate complete condition groups rather than requiring the learner to generate or derive them; the original question asks to state conditions, not to prove the amplitude formula. Distinguishing phase, path and zero-amplitude premises remains necessary.",
      "The node-spacing unit supplies both a distance and a ratio; it does not test independently writing the factor or a derivation. All four pairs have internally correct reciprocal arithmetic, so the standing-wave spacing cannot be inferred from arithmetic consistency alone.",
      "Standing-wave and diffraction units require multiple independent judgments, but do not elicit an exhaustive written comparison or a transmission/intensity model. These are not required by the original tasks."
    ],
    "acceptance_reason": "Each original conceptual target remains a distinct nontrivial response unit. Recognition and reasonable elimination are accepted for these short definition/condition questions because the decisive physical distinctions survive; no drafting/derivation ability is claimed. Ideal-model qualifications prevent the choice conversion from teaching universal false claims.",
    "cross_question_dependencies": "The interference definition supports subsequent phase and conservation reasoning, but does not state their answers. Standing-wave formation does not state the numerical adjacent-node spacing. The diffraction-description distractor in the interference item does not give the wavelength/size conditions of the diffraction item. The conservation stem rules out dissipative models but leaves two different 'No' explanations, requiring a conservation judgment rather than a polarity click.",
    "bilingual_equivalence": "The two complete learner sequences preserve option order, quantifiers, modes, all formulas, equal-frequency and fixed-phase distinctions, in-phase-source path premise, zero-minimum equal-amplitude premise, forward-envelope construction, time-averaged net transport and possibility rather than guaranteed brightness for diffraction. The English Huygens emitter distractor says 'every later wavefront' whereas Chinese says the later wavefront; both test the same invalid restriction of wavelet origins. No truth-relevant translation difference was observed.",
    "figure_and_metadata_scope": "All stems/options have empty figure_ids. The visible JSON and Markdown contain no source selectors, source-number mappings, key arrays, rationale metadata or source-solution links. No pixels were opened."
  },
  "important_qualifications": [
    "The phase/path extrema apply at given nonzero local component amplitudes; path formulas require explicitly in-phase sources/common wavelength, and a zero minimum additionally requires equal amplitudes.",
    "Cancellation alone is not dissipation or a local suspension of energy conservation; the complete field and energy flow matter.",
    "Huygens' forward-envelope construction is not a complete amplitude/backward-wave theory.",
    "Ideal standing waves have zero net time-averaged transport, not zero energy or zero instantaneous local flow.",
    "Adjacent nodes are separated by lambda/2 with lambda/d=2; arithmetic consistency alone cannot distinguish the proposed pairs.",
    "Diffraction claims compare the relevant obstructing transverse scale/opening width with wavelength and use possibility wording. Broad angular spreading does not guarantee strong transmission or brightness."
  ],
